格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"dsh-asc (full name DeepSeek Harness Agentic Surface Compaction) is a context-compaction plugin for DeepSeek Harness: the model itself decides when and what to compact, and every compaction decision is committed as a durable session-log replacement event (surfaceOp: replace) — rep","id":"gh:1334412967","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-asc","slug":"lmst2/dsh-asc","topics":["ai-agent","compaction","context-management","deepseek-harness","dsh-plugin"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"dsh-asc (full name DeepSeek Harness Agentic Surface Compaction) is a context-compaction plugin for D"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"eepSeek Harness: the model itself decides when and what to compact, and every compaction decision is"},{"id":"p1s3","text":" committed as a durable session-log replacement event (surfaceOp: replace) — rep"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-asc"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"English | 中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"**dsh-asc** (full name **DeepSeek Harness Agentic Surface Compaction**) is a\ncontext-compaction plug"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"in for\nDeepSeek Harness: **the\nmodel itself decides when and what to compact**, and every compaction"},{"id":"p4s3","text":" decision\nis committed as a durable session-log replacement event\n(`surfaceOp: replace`) — replayabl"},{"id":"p4s4","text":"e, searchable, and reversible."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Inspired by the model-driven compaction philosophy of\nopencode-acp, but built on\nDSH's event-sourced"},{"id":"p5s2","text":" log: compaction creates no side-state files,\ndecompression is log replay, and search covers the ful"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"l log including\ncompacted originals."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"**Prerequisites**: a working DeepSeek Harness\ninstallation (`dsh` CLI available); Node.js `^22.19` o"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"isites**: a working DeepSeek Harness\ninstallation (`dsh` CLI available); Node.js `^22.19` or `>=24`."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"**From npm** (recommended):"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"**From GitHub** — to use a commit newer than the npm release:"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"`dsh plugin` adds the plugin to the profile and enables it automatically\nbased on the `dsh.bundle` d"},{"id":"p12s2","text":"eclaration in the package; the tools and the\nsystem prompt load together with that profile."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"> **Restart required**: after installing, restart the running DeepSeek\n> Harness service."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"### Other install options"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"**From source** — to modify the plugin itself, or to contribute:"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"### Disabling the basic backend"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"`ctx.compaction` allows only one provider at a time. Disable the default\nbasic backend in your profi"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"le's own `cordis.patch.yml`:"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"Optionally mount the invariant companion and the full-text-search backend:"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"## Usage"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"After installing and restarting, no configuration is required — the plugin:"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"- injects the **context-management discipline** into the system prompt\n(judgment rules, tool usage, "},{"id":"p24s2","text":"tiered compaction cadence), so the model\nactively manages context from the very first turn;\n- inject"},{"id":"p24s3","text":"s **nudge prompts** on demand when context usage runs high (cadence-gated; iteration nudges addition"},{"id":"p24s4","text":"ally require real token growth — no per-turn nagging);\n- provides **deterministic degradation** (LLM"},{"id":"p24s5","text":" summarization, plus tool-result\npruning when the optional upstream pruner is mounted) on overflow o"},{"id":"p24s6","text":"r\nmanual compaction, without requiring model cooperation."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"The plugin provides five model tools:"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"| Tool | Purpose |"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"| `context_status` | context usage, tiered checkpoints, system/dialogue composition, recommended ran"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"ges, recent surface nodes |\n| `context_compress` | replace a surface range with a checkpoint you wri"},{"id":"p27s3","text":"te (batching supported; tool-call pairs auto-extended; quality gate) |\n| `context_decompress` | undo"},{"id":"p27s4","text":" a compaction: the original text returns to the surface at the checkpoint's own position (tier-aware"},{"id":"p27s5","text":"; `full: true` reaches raw content) |\n| `context_recap` | re-read checkpoint summaries without decom"},{"id":"p27s6","text":"pressing the originals |\n| `context_search` | full-text search over the whole log (including compact"},{"id":"p27s7","text":"originals |\n| `context_search` | full-text search over the whole log (including compacted content) |"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"Compacted content is never lost: the originals stay in the session log and\ncan be decompressed or se"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"s never lost: the originals stay in the session log and\ncan be decompressed or searched at any time."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"The system prompt ties the tools into one operating loop: capture consumed\nraw work into tier-1 chec"},{"id":"p29s2","text":"kpoints, distill settled tier-1 piles into tier-2\ndecisions and tier-2 piles into a tier-3 fact inde"},{"id":"p29s3","text":"x. Every checkpoint text\ncarries its topic and Compaction id, so when a visible summary already\npoin"},{"id":"p29s4","text":"ts at the needed detail the model decompresses that block directly;\n`context_search` is used only wh"},{"id":"p29s5","text":"en no visible summary says where a detail\nlives, and decompression always proceeds one tier at a tim"},{"id":"p29s6","text":" no visible summary says where a detail\nlives, and decompression always proceeds one tier at a time."},{"id":"p30s1","text":"## How it works"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"- **Event sourcing**: a compaction is a transaction in the log\n(`compaction/start` → `compaction/sum"},{"id":"p31s2","text":"mary` → replaced `user/message` →\n`compaction/end`); no side state.\n- **Tiered compaction**: checkpo"},{"id":"p31s3","text":"ints have tiers (T1 full detail → T2\ndistilled decisions → T3 bare facts); summaries get thinner as "},{"id":"p31s4","text":"they are\nreused.\n- **Reversible**: decompression replays the events shadowed in the log and\ncommits "},{"id":"p31s5","text":"one in-place replacement event; no side state is needed.\n- **Auditable**: who compacted what, the fu"},{"id":"p31s6","text":"ll summary text, and the token\ncost are all in the log."},{"id":"p32s1","text":"## Repository layout"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"## Documentation"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"| Doc | Contents |"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"| docs/usage.md | install, configuration, model experience, operations |\n| docs/design.md | implemen"},{"id":"p36s2","text":"ted contract: events, tools, automatic behavior, protection, invariants |\n| docs/analysis.md | compa"},{"id":"p36s3","text":"rison of DSH and opencode-acp context management |"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"## License"},{"id":"p38s1","text":"MIT. Algorithmic inspiration from\nDeepSeek Harness (MIT);\nonly the ideas of opencode-acp\n(AGPL) are "},{"id":"p38s2","text":"used, no source code. See NOTICE."}],"truncated":false}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
